# =============================================================================
# room_01.dialogue — ROOM 1: The Garden at Dusk. Ability: JUMP.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real writing from the design doc. Titles used by the room wiring:
#   ~ intro     played on room entry (auto zone)         — The Cat & The Weaver
#   ~ cat       played when you talk to Pip (grants Jump) — Pip
#   ~ complete  played when the maze is solved            — The Weaver, closing
# Edit freely; keep the title lines (~ ...) so the scene still finds them.
# =============================================================================


# --- OPENING CUTSCENE: The Cat & The Weaver --------------------------------
~ intro
The cat creeps in, chasing a single drifting strand of silk. It leads to the dark heart of the hedge. Something enormous shifts there. Only one long leg emerges into the light.
Weaver: ...So. The little ember comes. Closer. No — not too close. I am easier to bear in pieces. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_05.wav]
Cat: You're the one the others whisper about. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/cat/vox_cat_room_01_01.wav]
Weaver: I am the one the others whisper TO. There is a difference, though I'll not waste dusk explaining it. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_06.wav]
Weaver: You watch that window. Every evening. From exactly this far. [#highlight_window] [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_07.wav]
The cat says nothing.
Weaver: We watch it too. The girl there is kind to small frightened things — kinder than the world taught her to be. We have made her something. A thing of thread and patience. We hid it deep, where it would be safe. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_08.wav]
Weaver: Bring it back to her. You needn't know yet what it is. You need only know you're the right one to carry it. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_09.wav]
Cat: Why me? [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/cat/vox_cat_room_01_02.wav]
Weaver: ...You'll answer that yourself, by the end. Now. You've forgotten how to leave the ground. Someone here will remind you. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_10.wav]
=> END


# --- ABILITY CAT: Pip (grants JUMP) ----------------------------------------
~ cat
A kitten is bouncing off a mushroom for no reason at all, delighted every single time.
Pip: Hi hi hi! Did you SEE that?! I did it again! Watch — (boing) — AGAIN! [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/pip/vox_pip_room_01_11.wav]
Cat: I don't jump. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/cat/vox_cat_room_01_03.wav]
Pip: What? Everybody jumps. You're BUILT for it. Look at your legs! Those are jumping legs! [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/pip/vox_pip_room_01_12.wav]
Cat: It's a long way down. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/cat/vox_cat_room_01_04.wav]
Pip: Sure, but the good stuff's UP. You're not scared of falling. You're scared of being ALLOWED. It's okay. You're allowed. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/pip/vox_pip_room_01_13.wav]
Pip: Watch me, then copy me. The first one's the only hard one. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/pip/vox_pip_room_01_14.wav]
=> END


# --- CLOSING BEAT: The Weaver, on maze complete ----------------------------
~ complete
The silk gate unspools. The Weaver's voice drifts from nowhere and everywhere.
Weaver: One leap, and already higher than you've ever stood. Remember that, ember. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_15.wav]
Weaver: The ground lied to you about how far you could go. [#voice=res://audio_generation/output/voice/weaver/vox_weaver_room_01_16.wav]
=> END
